Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 00:50:46 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-117: margin adorners -- the selected one's
 distance to its container's edges (0.117.0)

WPF's design surface shows the selected element's margins: lines from the
element to its container's edges with the numbers. Here only the selection box
and the handles showed, the distance was in the properties. Now one selected
component (design mode) gets a thin line from its container's left edge and one
from the top edge, each with the distance -- its Left / Top, as the properties
say -- following a drag or a resize. None for the form, for several selected,
or with F9 (the element handles hidden).

Tests (all 4 layers pass: lib 162, smoke 192, panels, real VS Code 159):
probe (spbSave: 61 / 8, its style; none after F9; none for the form).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
